WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.624
Our toolkit measures length, mass, and time,

2
00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:05.763
and helps us investigate shapes.

3
00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:09.423
One meter is one hundred centimeters.

4
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:13.759
Half a meter is fifty centimeters.

5
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.148
Before adding lengths, use the same unit.

6
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.727
Two meters and thirty centimeters becomes two hundred plus thirty:

7
00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:27.154
two hundred thirty centimeters.

8
00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:34.926
One kilogram is one thousand grams.

9
00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:38.948
Half a kilogram is five hundred grams.

10
00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:43.847
Change kilograms into grams before combining them.

11
00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:47.881
One kilogram plus two hundred fifty grams

12
00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:51.030
makes one thousand two hundred fifty grams.

13
00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:55.998
An hour has sixty minutes.

14
00:00:57.600 --> 00:00:59.327
Count forward to find elapsed time.

15
00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:03.721
From nine forty to ten o’clock is twenty minutes.

16
00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:09.111
Continue five more minutes to ten oh five.

17
00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:14.331
Twenty plus five makes twenty-five minutes.

18
00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:21.323
A square has four equal sides and right angles,

19
00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:24.199
even when turned.

20
00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:27.512
A right angle is a square corner.

21
00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.324
This triangle has three equal sides and no right angle.

22
00:01:37.429 --> 00:01:38.400
Does it fit either rule?

23
00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:42.807
Neither.

24
00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:47.796
Match your units, count time carefully,

25
00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:51.810
and check shape properties instead of guessing from appearance.

26
00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:56.603
Take your time, and try the Unit Three quizzes!
